      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "0ce7d6bd509a20ecdb88225be38469e1dbdb3077",
            "subject": "LU-20076 tests: make target start cheaper"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 01:39:51.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-04 06:16:47.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: make conf-sanity 35a reach MDT0000",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: make conf-sanity 35a reach MDT0000\n\ntest_35a stops and restarts MDT0000 with a df running, then\nlooks in the client debug log for the server the client\ntried first when it reconnected. With several MDTs, df's\nstatfs can be answered by any one of them, so nothing makes\nthe client notice that MDT0000 went away. When the restart\nis quick the client has not reconnected by the time the log\nis read, no connection line is found, and the test fails\nwith \"Tried to connect to  not last active server\". This\nhappens every time on a VM cluster with 4 MDTs, where\nMDT0000 restarts in under a second.\n\nUse \"lfs df\", which sends a statfs to every MDT and waits\nfor each to answer, so the client reconnects to MDT0000\nbefore the test reads the log.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=35a,ONLY_REPEAT=5\nTest-Parameters: mdtcount=4 testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=35a,ONLY_REPEAT=5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: If23943a4a611e95217d571555e2d5ad301a44f86\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
